---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout title="About Calculator Street — Free Construction Calculators" description="About Calculator Street: US-focused, fast & private calculators for construction. Static, no tracking, built for homeowners & contractors.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] pt-6">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">About Calculator Street</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body [text-wrap:pretty]">Calculator Street (CalculatorSt.com) is a complete construction and home-improvement calculator platform — focused, accurate and private. We cover concrete, gravel, rebar, masonry, roofing, flooring, framing, decking, fencing, landscaping, asphalt and more. Every calculator is hand-verified for US customary and metric units, with clear formulas, worked examples and waste-aware estimates.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Founded 2026 by <span class="font-medium text-ink">Vipul Otari</span> — built for US homeowners and contractors working with US customary units and metric equivalents. Every calculation runs in your browser, no data is sent to any server. Last updated: <span class="font-mono text-xs">2026-09-22</span>.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
        <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-white " aria-hidden="true">VO</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Vipul Otari — Author & Lead Reviewer</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Built and reviewed every calculator. Mathematical models, example tables and construction assumptions are documented on each calculator page with cited sources. Contact for technical feedback or corrections: <a href="mailto:hello@calculatorst.com" class="text-link underline">hello@calculatorst.com</a>.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Editorial standard: Calculations cite their sources on each page. References include engineering organizations, government agencies, and manufacturer technical data where applicable.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 ">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Our principles</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Client-side computing</span> — all math and dimensional conversions execute locally in your browser. Your measurements and cost inputs are never sent to our servers.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">US & Metric standards</span> — feet, inches, yards, and short tons (2,000 lb), with precise SI metric equivalents based on NIST SP 811 international conversion factors.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Mobile-first</span> — large inputs, thumb-friendly, works on the job site at 320px. No horizontal scroll.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Transparent</span> — every page shows formulas, examples, assumptions and related calculators. Sources are cited on individual calculator pages where relevant — concrete calculators cite concrete industry sources, roofing calculators cite roofing sources, etc.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">How we verify</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-body">Unit conversions use NIST SP 811 exact factors (1 ft = 0.3048 m, 1 lb = 0.45359237 kg). Density values and bag yields are sourced from manufacturer documentation and public resources. Waste factors are based on common construction practice (10% standard, 15% curves/irregular). Each calculator page documents its specific assumptions and sources.</p>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Library</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-body">The platform now includes a complete library of construction and home-improvement calculators — organized into sixteen focused categories and searchable from any page. Every calculator is a standalone, indexable tool with its own formula, example, diagram and related tools.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Questions? <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
